  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Norleucine and Jurkat cells, mediated through Calmodulin. Norleucine is linked to Calmodulin, which is a key regulatory protein involved in cellular signaling and calcium-dependent processes. Calmodulin is also a target of another compound, 19-Oxo-3-beta,5,14-trihydroxy-5-beta-bufa-20,22-dienolide-3-acetate, which is itself targeted by Jurkat cells. This indicates a possible pathway where Norleucine may influence Calmodulin activity, which in turn could modulate Jurkat cell function. The scores from the two paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Norleucine and Jurkat, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the role of Calmodulin and the specific molecular interactions involved.",
